ID@XBOX x IGN Showcase Recap: All the News and Announcements
We&#8217;ve just wrapped up another fantastic ID@XBOX and IGN Showcase, bringing the latest news and updates on many brilliant indie titles heading to XBOX&nbsp;– from world premieres and long-awaited announcements to a fresh wave of titles making their way to Game Pass. We even threw in a surprise launch!&nbsp;
The show included the reveal of A Game About Digging a Hole Together , the sequel to the popular subterranean sandbox adventure, and Magenta Down, a new sci-fi adventure. We also announced that several&nbsp;CRITICAL REFLEX&nbsp;titles are heading to XBOX soon, including the frosty cooking sim, Arctic Eggs , which is available today!&nbsp;
Many of the ID@XBOX games featured during today&#8217;s showcase will also support XBOX Play Anywhere at launch – so you can enjoy them across console and PC at no additional cost.&nbsp;
Check out the full recap of everything shown during the event below!&nbsp;
Revealed during today’s ID@XBOX and IGN show, A Game About Digging A Hole Together is a minimalist experience about digging a hole at the beach, now with friends. Dig together, collect resources, sell them, upgrade your equipment and search for a promised treasure buried deep beneath the sand. A Game About Digging A Hole Together is heading to XBOX Series X|S, XBOX on PC, and Game Pass on December 4, 2026.&nbsp;
Chronoscript: The Endless End is an innovative, exploration-based action-adventure game comprised of two worlds: a 3D rendered grand residence littered with thousands of manuscript pages, and the 2D pen-and-ink illustrated worlds within them. Face off against the Ruined, twisted remnants of those who lost their lives in the waking world. Grow stronger through exploration and battle, and immerse yourself in the winding narrative of the Immortal Vampire and her Editor. A unique approach to spatial perspective awaits you. Chronoscript: The Endless End arrives summer 2027 for XBOX Series X|S and XBOX on PC.&nbsp;
Tongue-grapple and pinball-bounce the frog prince across levels to reach the Witch’s Banquet in this hand-drawn 2D precision platformer. Each whimsical world has its own wacky boss, hidden collectibles, and a unique traversal ability. Hungry for a little competition? Take on your friends and the fastest frogs in the world on the online speedrunning leaderboard. CROAK will be available March 2027 for XBOX Series X|S, XBOX on PC, day one with Game Pass, and supports XBOX Play Anywhere.&nbsp;
